  "next_action": "Merge PR #10 (Phase 3) and this Phase 4 PR (branch claude/m3-dvp-phase4). DvP research then waits for the 2026 regular season to end: rebuild targets with 2026, add a prospective stage that verifies the frozen method hashes against the new targets, score 2026 weeks 12-18 (PROSPECTIVE_2026.md). Meanwhile resume M3 slices 3c-3e and weather W1.",
  "sections": {
    "review": {
      "summary": "Read the specification's Phase 4 (frozen manifest, CONDITIONALLY_HELD_OUT labeling, prospective confirmation, decision labels per position and globally) and section 12, the Phase 3 receipts and frozen candidates, and the stage guard. 2025 exposure: descriptive only (v0 and Phase A used 2016-2025 for repeatability); no 2025 forecast, outcome or parameter entered model selection, which used development folds 2017-2023 and was confirmed on 2024.",
      "files": [
        "config/dvp/backtest.json",
        "scripts/model/dvp.py",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/dvp/walkforward.py"
      ]
    },
    "plan": {
      "summary": "1) dvp.py freeze writes config/dvp/frozen.json: SHA-256 of the method files (walkforward.py, lab.py, asof.py, observations.py, dvp.py, base/backtest configs, frozen candidates), the audit run's output hashes and targets index, the protocol (RMSE, week-block bootstrap, seed, practical minimum) and the decision rule, plus the prospective 2026 window. 2) backtest --stage holdout runs only when every frozen hash matches the files on disk; parameters fit on 2016-2024; candidates evaluated on 2025; decisions by the predeclared rule (PROMISING if the candidate is a DvP variant meeting the minimum in development, validation and holdout; NOT_USEFUL if the best DvP misses the minimum in all three; INCONCLUSIVE otherwise; BLOCKED on any integrity failure). 3) Tests for the holdout guard. 4) MODEL_CARD.md, PROSPECTIVE_2026.md, registry decisions, records.",
      "files": [
        "scripts/model/dvp.py",
        "config/dvp/frozen.json",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/dvp/walkforward.py",
        "libs/arbit-model/tests/test_dvp_walkforward.py"
      ]
    },
    "implementation": {
      "summary": "walkforward: check_stage admits the holdout only as a verified holdout stage; decide() applies the predeclared rule. dvp.py: freeze (method and config hashes, audit outputs, targets index, protocol, decision rule, periods, prospective window from the schedule; refuses uncommitted code and mismatched candidates); backtest --stage holdout (verifies every frozen hash first, coverage check, decisions per position and overall); registry record M3-3-HOLDOUT-2025; report plot with all three periods. Runs: freeze at f75868b (2026-11-24 03:16 UTC, prospective 2026 weeks 12-18), holdout at 165d140 (all hashes verified), report and registry afterwards (dvp.py changed only in registry and plot order after the holdout).",
      "files": [
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/dvp/walkforward.py",
        "libs/arbit-model/tests/test_dvp_walkforward.py",
        "scripts/model/dvp.py",
        "config/dvp/frozen.json",
        "config/dvp/backtest.json"
      ]
    },
    "validation": {
      "summary": "Checks: foundation, model tests (125), point-in-time, ruff check and format, mypy, the full Python suite: all exit 0. Holdout guard tests: holdout refused without a verified manifest and outside the holdout stage (T18); decision rule unit-tested for every label. The holdout receipt records the frozen manifest hash (1ef59583) and code 165d140; every frozen hash was verified before forecasting; coverage complete (3,256 forecasts = every valid 2025 cell). Freeze cross-checked the candidates against the development receipt and the validation receipt's candidates hash. Model card and report numbers checked against the receipt (one overstatement about unshrunk D/ST corrected).",
      "files": [
        "libs/arbit-model/tests/test_dvp_walkforward.py",
